---
import Case from '../../layouts/Case.astro';
import Plate from '../../components/Plate.astro';
import Activity from '../../components/Activity.astro';
import activity from '../../data/cases/sambadeiras-activity.json';
---

<Case
  title="Sambadeiras"
  summary="Check-in, attendance and payments for a women's samba group in Olinda, built for whatever phone each member has and for a loud, crowded rehearsal."
  facts={[
    { label: 'Client', value: "A women's samba group, Olinda (PE)" },
    { label: 'My role', value: 'Product, design, development, operations' },
    { label: 'Timeline', value: 'Jul 2025 – today' },
    { label: 'Stack', value: 'Ruby on Rails 8, Hotwire, PostgreSQL, Asaas, Fly.io' },
    { label: 'Status', value: 'In use by the group' },
  ]}
  links={[]}
>
  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="brief">
    <h2 id="brief">The brief</h2>
    <div class="case-body">
      <p>
        The group brings together women from very different backgrounds, on very different phones,
        with very different comfort with technology. Every one of them had to be able to check in
        at each rehearsal from her own phone, and the board needed to manage monthly fees, costume
        payments and contact details without spreadsheets.
      </p>
      <p>
        That set the bar: the check-in has to work on an old Android in bright sun, with music
        playing, for someone who has never installed an app like it. Everything else comes second.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="work">
    <h2 id="work">What I built</h2>
    <ol class="decisions">
      <li>
        <h3>Check-in in one scan</h3>
        <p>
          Every rehearsal or parade gets its own QR code. A member scans it with the phone camera or the
          in-app scanner and confirms with one tap. The flow is designed around a check-in of under ten
          seconds.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>A location check that never locks anyone out</h3>
        <p>
          Check-ins are compared with a radius around the venue. The board chooses whether to reject
          check-ins from outside it or just flag them for reports. When a phone refuses to share its
          location, the check-in still goes through and is marked, so an old phone or a denied
          permission never costs anyone her attendance.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Payments the members choose themselves</h3>
        <p>
          Members pick PIX or credit card, paid in full or in instalments (six for the yearly fee, three
          for the costume). Exemptions follow each member's enrolment type. Charges go through
          <strong>Asaas</strong>, and its webhooks update each payment's status. The board charges the
          month with one button that is safe to press twice, and can reissue a charge, cancelling the old one along with its fines.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Tools for the board</h3>
        <p>
          The board records justified absences and manages members, sections and activities. Members
          see their own attendance and payment history.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li>
        <h3>Built for the phones people actually have</h3>
        <p>
          Pages are server-rendered with light JavaScript, touch targets are large, contrast holds
          outdoors, and all copy is written in Portuguese from the start. Five decision records
          document the payment and testing design, and the system tests run fully isolated from the
          payment provider.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="plates">
    <h2 id="plates">The app</h2>
    <div class="plate-groups">
      <p class="plate-note">Screens captured from the running app with invented members and payments.</p>
      <div class="plates plates--phones">
        <Plate
          number={1}
          frame="phone"
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/checkin-landing.webp"
          width={780}
          height={796}
          alt="Check-in landing page for 'Ensaio geral', with date, time and venue, a note that the location was found, and a Confirmar check-in button."
          caption="After scanning the rehearsal's QR code: one button to confirm."
        />
        <Plate
          number={2}
          frame="phone"
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/checkin-done.webp"
          width={780}
          height={1036}
          alt="Check-in confirmation: a green tick and 'Você já fez check-in!' for Ensaio geral."
          caption="Done. Scanning again just shows this confirmation."
        />
        <Plate
          number={3}
          frame="phone"
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/checkin-no-location.webp"
          width={780}
          height={836}
          alt="Check-in landing page noting that location is unavailable and the check-in will be recorded without it."
          caption="No location from the phone? The check-in still goes through, marked for the board."
        />
      </div>
      <div class="plates plates--phones">
        <Plate
          number={4}
          frame="phone"
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/payment-plan.webp"
          width={780}
          height={1026}
          alt="Payment step of the profile: monthly fee set to PIX in six instalments of R$120, costume set to card in three instalments of R$155, and costume size."
          caption="Each member picks her own plan: PIX or card, in full or in instalments."
        />
        <Plate
          number={5}
          frame="phone"
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/financeiro.webp"
          width={780}
          height={1510}
          alt="Financeiro page: an alert for two late payments, the amount open, and charges with Pendente, Atrasado and Pago statuses and Pagar buttons."
          caption="Her payments: what's open, what's late, one tap to pay."
        />
        <Plate
          number={6}
          frame="phone"
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/frequencia.webp"
          width={780}
          height={1744}
          alt="Frequência page: 12 attendances out of 15 activities, with rehearsals marked Presente, Faltou or Falta justificada."
          caption="Her attendance, including absences the board has justified."
        />
      </div>
      <div class="plates plates--wide">
        <Plate
          number={7}
          zoom
          src="/cases/sambadeiras/cobranca.webp"
          width={1600}
          height={1553}
          alt="Board view of September 2026 payments: totals of paid, open and late fees and costumes, the processing history of each charge run with totals and failures, and a table of members' charges with Regerar buttons."
          caption="The board's month: charge runs with their results, every member's status, and a button to reissue a charge."
        />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="case-section" aria-labelledby="shipped">
    <h2 id="shipped">What shipped</h2>
    <div class="case-body">
      <ul class="shipped">
        <li>In use by the group for check-ins, attendance and payments, with feedback from both members and the board built back in.</li>
        <li><strong>Asaas payments</strong> covering PIX and card, up-front and instalment plans, exemptions and batch charging.</li>
        <li><strong>119 commits</strong> since July 2025, with five architecture decision records.</li>
      </ul>
      <Activity data={activity} label="Commits per week" />
    </div>
  </section>
</Case>

<style>
  .plate-groups {
    display: grid;
    gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
  }

  .plate-note {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-style: italic;
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }
</style>
